a list: a,b | sent GET /todos
two views asking at once: a,b | sent GET /todos
a row by its key: 1:a | sent GET /todos/1
another key: 2:a | sent GET /todos/2
order and a default written out are one ask: GET /todos?done=true&limit=10&title=a
a null member and an absent one are one ask: GET /todos?limit=10&title=a
different values are different asks, escaped: GET /todos?limit=10&title=a | GET /todos?limit=11&title=a | GET /todos?done=false&limit=10&title=a | GET /todos?limit=10&title=a%20b%26c
a nested record cannot be a query: failed `by` is nested, and a path or a query carries text, numbers and flags | sent 
a create is a body in name order: 9:new | sent POST /todos {"done":false,"id":0,"title":"new"}
an update fills the key's hole and leaves it out of the body: 5:a | sent PATCH /todos/5 {"done":true,"title":"edited"}
a read sent and a write asked are refused: failed `ask` reads, and POST /todos writes: use `send` | failed `send` writes, and GET /todos reads: use `ask` | sent 
a text key is one escaped segment: sent GET /notes/a%2Fb%20c
a hole with no value is refused in words: failed the route's `slug` has no value in its args | sent 
a removal is sent by the key: taken | sent DELETE /todos/4
